{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "LANDMARKS — ten famous places, six themes, deliberately unsubtle.",
    "",
    "Built for hearing the engine work rather than for listening to. Every",
    "landmark below hands over to a whole different theme, so jumping between",
    "the saved places in Explore should be immediately obvious: Paris is an",
    "accordion waltz, Broadway is brass stabs, Shibuya is fast neon, the Grand",
    "Canyon is almost nothing at all.",
    "",
    "HOW TO USE IT",
    "  Import, then Anywhere -> tap a saved place. Give it two or three seconds",
    "  to take hold. The line under the theme selector tells you which theme is",
    "  playing and which cue is holding it.",
    "",
    "  The selector still shows YOUR choice and goes dim while a cue overrides",
    "  it. That is expected — the cue wins while you are standing there, and",
    "  your choice comes back when you leave.",
    "",
    "WHAT PLAYS WHERE",
    "  Eiffel Tower           Paris     accordion, triplet lilt, warm",
    "  Broadway / Times Sq    Broadway  brass stabs, showy, fast",
    "  Shibuya Crossing       Neon      fast blips, tight, pentatonic",
    "  Colosseum              Ancient   vast, phrygian, frame drum",
    "  Machu Picchu           Ancient   same, but thinner air",
    "  Grand Canyon           Vast      drone and swells, almost still",
    "  Golden Gate Bridge     Vast      same, with fog horns",
    "  White House            Stately   ceremonial brass and timpani",
    "  Sydney Opera House     Stately   brighter, orchestral",
    "  Abbey Road             (layers)  a backbeat over whatever is playing",
    "",
    "All music here is original. These are impressions of places, not",
    "arrangements of anything associated with them.",
    "",
    "The radii are generous — 400 m at most landmarks, 3 km at the Grand",
    "Canyon, because the place is the size of the place."
  ],

